00:57:39.910 --> 00:57:47.130
<v Ira Glass>WBEZ management oversight by Torey Malatia, who meets with his music staff every single week, looks at their playlists, and declares--
<v Ira Glass>WBEZ管理监督托雷·马拉蒂亚，他每周都会与音乐人员开会，查看他们的播放列表，并宣布——

00:57:47.130 --> 00:57:54.180
<v Ellery Eskelin>This music has everything in the world going against it. It's completely artificial. It's a scam.
<v Ellery Eskelin>这种音乐有一切不利因素。它完全是人工的，是个骗局。

00:57:54.180 --> 00:58:55.420
<v Ira Glass>And we started today's program with Leonardo da Vinci. Let's end with Leonardo as well. This is a quote from one of his notebooks. "To the ambitious, for whom neither the bounty of life nor the beauty of the world suffice to content, it comes as penance that life for them is squandered and that they possess neither the benefits nor the beauty of the world. And if they are unable to perceive what is divine in nature, which is all around them, how will they be able to see their own divinity, which is sometimes hidden?" I'm Ira Glass, back next week with more stories of This American Life.
<v Ira Glass>我们以列奥纳多·达·芬奇开始了今天的节目。让我们也以列奥纳多作为结束。这是他笔记本中的一句话：“对于那些雄心勃勃的人来说，世间的富足和世界的美丽都无法使之满足，对他们来说，这是一种惩罚，因为他们虚度了生命，既没有享受到世间的利益，也没有感受到世界的美丽。如果他们无法感知周围神圣的大自然，他们又怎能看到自己内心有时隐藏的神性呢？”我是艾拉·格拉斯，下周带回更多《这就是美国生活》的故事。

00:58:55.420 --> 00:59:00.420
<v Announcer>PRI. Public Radio International.
<v Announcer>PRI。国际公共广播电台。
